# Anchored at the root only, which missed the two crates outside the workspace:
# vleo-wasm and vleo-py build into their own target/ directories, and staging
# them adds several thousand build artefacts to a commit.
/target
**/target/
/generated
**/*.rs.bk
.DS_Store
node_modules
*.pyc
__pycache__

# The local data store. `VLEO_DATA` normally puts it under $HOME, outside any
# checkout -- but the devcontainer deliberately points it at
# ${containerWorkspaceFolder}/.vleo/data so a Codespace keeps its store beside
# the workspace. That put a generated directory inside the working tree, and
# nothing ignored it, so the first run of the daemon in a Codespace reported
# ten untracked "changes" that are not changes: `vleo.lock` plus a byte copy of
# bundles/solar-weather/2026.09.14, which the store syncs from `bundles/` when
# it opens empty. The shipped bundle is the tracked copy and the one with
# provenance; committing the store would make a second copy of the same
# reference data with none, which is the thing bundles/README.md exists to
# prevent.
/.vleo/
